Z||000002||fierobear||10-17-2001||11:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Out of 2000 Indy's, 200 were manuals and 1800 were automatics.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've heard that it's more like 50/50. Hell, I've got 2 manuals. Wanna buy them?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-17-2001||01:41 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Out of 2000 Indy's, 200 were manuals and 1800 were automatics.<P>From Fierobear,<P>I've heard that it's more like 50/50. Hell, I've got 2 manuals. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I searched around, I cannot find any reference to say how many were built with which trans. I know the "popular" opinion is the numbers above, But on page 70 of G. Wirtzenburg's book "Fiero", it states:<P>"Most Indy Pace-Car replica's had the 4-speed 4:10 and some were automatics"<P>I would guess the statement says that there are more manual trans cars then auto's.<P>So lets take a poll.<P>I know Bob Steiger has 3 Indy's<BR>2 man and 1 Auto<BR>Haze has 1 auto<BR>Coyote has 1 auto<P>So far that's 2 for manual and 3 for auto.<BR>any more?<P><BR>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-17-2001||03:13 PM||||This gets hashed around every so often....the truth is no one really knows.<P>The 200 manual/1800 auto. thing makes absolutely no sense to me......I have seen way too many 4-sp. Indy's for this to be true.  I think someone way back when pulled this number out of their butt to make their Indy (that they were selling) seem more "rare" than it really was.<P>It makes sense that the Indy production was no different than the rest of the '84 Fieros and about half were 4-sp. and half were auto.  I don't have the exact % breakdown for the '84 in front of me, but generally speaking (in all years) half were autos and half were sticks (give or take a few %).<P>Then there is the debate on how many Indys were even built.  I have heard that there were fewer than 2000 built, 2000 built and that there were 2000 US cars and an additional 50 Canadian versions, etc.  <P>Again, in my opinion, there is no concrete evidence either way as to how many of each tranny exists (or how many Indys exist), so I tend to not believe anyone who claims that there were only "X" 4-speeds or "Y" autos.  <P>I know this doesn't help you out, but again, there just isn't any hard numbers out there. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||10-17-2001||03:20 PM||||MrFiero, I agree. Too bad Pontiac didn't have a special VIN code just for Indy's. From what I've read thru VIN decoder sites, the Indy's were VIN'd as SE's. I know the First Indy built VIN # but I don't know the last. Although this won't help because it obvious that they didn't build the Indy's in in a row. They were intermixed with the rest of the cars.||||reg||1
